    "title": "Spotswood boys soccer edges William Monroe | Spotswood | dnronline.com",
    "text": "Spotswood remained unbeaten in Valley District play after a 1-0 shutout of William Monroe on Wednesday in Penn Laird.\nSenior midfielder Beckham Hash delivered the golden goal off an assist from sophomore Paywand Muhamed.\nIn goal, junior Daniel Gulino posted seven saves in the shutout.\nThe Trailblazers (2-3, 2-0 Valley) will return to action Friday at district opponent Broadway.",
